{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3Braid","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3Braid","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalParam"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.hrel_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.hrel_col","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/Orbit3Braid.lean#L165-L173","doc":"**The parameter relation, column-domino.**  With `a₂ = a(d+1)` at `x/q²` and\n`sc = -q⁻¹`, the same relation holds — which is why `genA_genB_braid` is stated through\n`sc` rather than through `q`: the `q`-only form covers the row case only. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.hrel_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.hrel_row","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/Orbit3Braid.lean#L156-L163","doc":"**The parameter relation, row-domino.**  With `a₁ = a(d)` at `x` and `a₂ = a(d-1)` at\n`q²x`, the relation `a₂ · sc · (sc - a₁) = a₁` of `genA_genB_braid` holds identically for\n`sc = q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.hsc_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.hsc_col","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/Orbit3Braid.lean#L151-L154","doc":"The **column-domino scalar** `-q⁻¹` satisfies the same quadratic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.hsc_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.hsc_row","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/Orbit3Braid.lean#L146-L149","doc":"The **row-domino scalar** `q` satisfies the Hecke quadratic `sc² = c·sc + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.genA_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.genA_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/Orbit3Braid.lean#L120-L131","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic relation on the orbit** for `ρ(σ_k)`.  The `2 × 2` block gives it\nby Cayley–Hamilton (trace `c`, determinant `-1`); the scalar entry needs `hsc`, which is\nprecisely the statement that `sc` is an eigenvalue of a Hecke generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.genA_genB_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.genA_genB_braid","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/Orbit3Braid.lean#L99-L118","doc":"**The size-`3` orbit braid identity (Yang–Baxter).**\n\n`ρ(σ_k) ρ(σ_{k+1}) ρ(σ_k) = ρ(σ_{k+1}) ρ(σ_k) ρ(σ_{k+1})` on a size-`3` orbit — a domino\nplus a disjoint cell — given that the scalar satisfies the Hecke quadratic and that the two\nblock parameters satisfy the relation forced by their shared axial distance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.genB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.genB","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/Orbit3Braid.lean#L86-L97","doc":"`ρ(σ_{k+1})` on the same orbit: a `2 × 2` block on `{0,1}` with parameter `a₂`, and the\nscalar `sc` on filling `2`.  The block sits on a **different** summand from `genA`'s — that\nis what makes the orbit irreducible to the `2 × 2` case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.genA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Orbit3.genA","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/Orbit3Braid.lean#L73-L84","doc":"`ρ(σ_k)` on a size-`3` orbit: the scalar `sc` on filling `0`, a `2 × 2` block on\n`{1,2}` with parameter `a₁`.  Defined by a match on the index values rather than as a\n`!![…]` literal — see the performance note in `Orbit6Braid`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}